## Setting Up Fuzz Testing

### Project Structure
```
my_project/
├── src/
│   └── lib.xi
├── fuzz/
│   ├── fuzz_targets/
│   │   └── parse_config.xi
│   └── corpus/
│       └── parse_config/
│           └── seed1.txt
└── xiom.toml
```

### Writing a Fuzz Target
```xiom
// fuzz/fuzz_targets/parse_config.xi

#[fuzz_target]
fn fuzz_parse_config(data: &[Byte]) -> Unit {
  // Step 1: Convert bytes to your input type
  let input = Str.from_utf8(data);
  if input.is_err() { return; }

  // Step 2: Call the function under test
  // Contract violations here = bugs found!
  let result = parse_config(input.unwrap());

  // Step 3: Optionally check invariants
  match result {
    Ok(config) => {
      assert(config.port > 0);
      assert(config.port <= 65535);
    },
    Err(_) => {},  // Parse errors are expected
  }
}
```

### Running the Fuzzer
```sh
# Build and run the fuzzer
xiom fuzz run parse_config

# Run with specific options
xiom fuzz run parse_config -- -max_len=4096 -timeout=30

# Minimize a crashing input
xiom fuzz minimize parse_config crash-001.bin
```

### Corpus Seeding
```sh
# Create seed corpus directory
mkdir -p fuzz/corpus/parse_config

# Add representative inputs
echo "port=8080" > fuzz/corpus/parse_config/seed1.txt
echo "host=localhost port=3000" > fuzz/corpus/parse_config/seed2.txt
```

